---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import chrisDuffSource from '../assets/chris-duff-source.jpg';
import { CONTACT_HREF, NAV_HREFS } from '../data/nav';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About - Excel Automate | Hobart"
  description="Chris Duff has been building tools and automations in Excel for 25 years. Excel Automate brings that to businesses and non-profits across Australia."
  current="About"
>
  <section class="prose-section" style="background: var(--page);">
    <div class="about-hero" data-reveal="hero">
      <div>
        <h1 class="hero-heading">Nice to <span class="accent">meet</span> you</h1>
        <div class="hero-rule"></div>
        <p class="hero-standfirst" style="margin-bottom: 22px;">
          Excel Automate is freshly sprung in Hobart, but the person behind it has been around a while.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 19px); line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0; text-wrap: pretty;">
          Hi, I'm <span class="accent" style="font-weight: 700;">Chris</span>. I've been building tools and automations in
          Excel for 25 years across a range of different organisations, picking up plenty of database and CRM knowledge
          along the way. A degree in software engineering was the starting point, and experience has taught me a lot
          since.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-photo">
        <Image
          src={chrisDuffSource}
          alt="Chris Duff"
          width={620}
          format="webp"
          class="about-photo-img"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section" style="background: var(--tint);">
    <div class="prose-col" data-reveal="origin">
      <h2>Where I'm coming from</h2>
      <p>
        A lot of my recent work has been with non-profit organisations, where money is better spent on doing good than
        on sophisticated systems and large IT teams. The downside I've seen is that a lot of tasks get stuck being done
        the slow manual way, which has its own costs over time.
      </p>
      <p>
        With a business focused on finding fast and efficient custom solutions - something that
        <span class="accent">Modern Excel</span> is perfect for - I'm aiming to help more organisations across Australia
        save time, costs, and headaches.
      </p>
      <p>Being based in Hobart, I'm also keen to work with any businesses in Tasmania who might be dealing with similar issues.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section" style="background: var(--page);">
    <div class="prose-col" data-reveal="about">
      <h2>What I'm about</h2>
      <p>
        I always enjoy solving problems, but the part of this work I like best isn't the code and the data. It's
        working with the <span class="accent">people</span> who use the systems day in day out, who labour over data and
        wrestle with spreadsheets.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px);">
        Not everyone has time to become an expert at Excel, and if I can do my part to make the job easier, they can
        focus on all the other things they do to bring value.
      </p>
      <div class="pulled-quote closing">
        <p>And that's a pretty good outcome.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band cta-band--green">
    <div class="cta-band-inner" data-reveal="cta">
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p data-fit-text="Think we might be able to help with something?" data-fit-group="cta-contact">
        Think we might be able to help with something?
      </p>
      <a href={CONTACT_HREF} class="btn btn-solid-inverse">Get in touch</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band cta-band--dark">
    <div class="cta-band-inner" data-reveal="ctaLearn">
      <h2>Learn more</h2>
      <p>Enough about me! Learn more about Excel and how we use it.</p>
      <a href={NAV_HREFS['Our approach']} class="btn btn-ghost">Learn more</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script src="../scripts/cta-fit.js"></script>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    max-width: var(--w-prose);
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 310px;
    gap: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 44px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .about-photo {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 310px;
    justify-self: end;
    /* Optical alignment: the h1's glyphs start below the top of its line box
       (Manrope 800 / line-height 1.08 puts the cap height ~0.197x font-size
       down), so a box-aligned photo reads as sitting high without this nudge
       — see Design Decisions - About page.md. */
    margin-top: calc(clamp(38px, 5.2vw, 58px) * 0.2);
  }
  .about-photo-img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 30%;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: var(--icon-tile);
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .about-hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .about-photo {
      justify-self: start;
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
